§§ `s 6 -- entitlement`

-- From 1 January 2018: 1 January 2018 to 31 December 2024, both counted, is 2557 days (7 x 365 + 29 February 2020 and
-- 2024), exactly the 7 years to 1 January 2025. 1/60th of 2557 days is 2557 / 420 weeks (about 6.088).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 31 12 2024) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 30 12 2024) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 31 12 2024) 0 0 EQUALS 2557 DIVIDED BY 420
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 30 12 2024) 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- One week that does not count pushes the 7 years back a week: 7 January 2025.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 31 12 2024) 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 6 1 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 7 1 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 7 1 2025) 1 0 EQUALS 2557 DIVIDED BY 420
-- 10 years from 1 July 2015 to 30 June 2025: 3653 days (3 leap days), 3653 / 420 weeks (about 8.698); less 2 weeks taken,
-- 2813 / 420; less 10 weeks taken, nothing left.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 0 EQUALS 3653 DIVIDED BY 420
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 2 EQUALS 2813 DIVIDED BY 420
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 10 EQUALS 0
-- Counted from 29 February 2016: the 7 years to 28 February 2023 are 2556 days, so they are completed with 27 February 2023
-- counted (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 29 2 2016) (`d` 27 2 2023) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave yet` (`d` 29 2 2016) (`d` 26 2 2023) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 7 -- public holidays and annual leave`

-- 1 June to 12 July 2026 is 42 days: 6 weeks; with one public holiday 41 / 7; with five days of annual leave as well 36 / 7.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave does the period use` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 12 7 2026) 0 0 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave does the period use` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 12 7 2026) 1 0 EQUALS 41 DIVIDED BY 7
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave does the period use` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 12 7 2026) 1 5 EQUALS 36 DIVIDED BY 7

§§ `s 8(3) -- leave in advance`

-- Ending before 7 years: none of the advance leave was ever earned; the whole $6000 may be deducted.
#ASSERT `How much of my advance leave pay can be deducted` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 30 6 2023) 0 0 4 6000 EQUALS 6000
-- Ending after 8 years (1 January 2018 to 31 December 2025, 2922 days, 2922 / 420 weeks earned): of 8 weeks in advance,
-- 8 - 2922/420 = 438/420 weeks were not earned; 12000 x (438/420) / 8 = 10950 / 7 (about $1564.29).
#ASSERT `How much of my advance leave pay can be deducted` (`d` 1 1 2018) (`d` 31 12 2025) 0 0 8 12000 EQUALS 10950 DIVIDED BY 7
-- Ending after 10 years with 4 weeks in advance: all earned, nothing deducted. No advance leave: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much of my advance leave pay can be deducted` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 0 4 6000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my advance leave pay can be deducted` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

