§§ `s 16 -- normal weekly hours (formulas F1 to F3)`

-- F1: (1800 + 152) / (52 - 2) = 39.04. F2: (9500 + 760) / (260 - 10) = 41.04. F3: (15000 + 1200) / (420 - 20) = 40.5.
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(a) -- the 52-week average` 1800 152 2 EQUALS JUST 39.04
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(b) -- the 260-week average` 9500 760 10 EQUALS JUST 41.04
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(c) -- the whole-period average` 15000 1200 420 20 EQUALS JUST 40.5
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(a) -- the 52-week average` 0 0 52 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(b) -- the 260-week average` 0 0 260 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(2)(c) -- the whole-period average` 0 0 20 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No hours fixed: the greatest, 41.04.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` FALSE 0 FALSE 1800 152 2 9500 760 10 15000 1200 420 20 EQUALS JUST 41.04
-- Hours fixed at 38 and unchanged: 38. Fixed but changed in the last 104 weeks: the greatest average, 41.04.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` TRUE 38 FALSE 1800 152 2 9500 760 10 15000 1200 420 20 EQUALS JUST 38
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` TRUE 38 TRUE 1800 152 2 9500 760 10 15000 1200 420 20 EQUALS JUST 41.04
-- A whole year of unpaid leave in the last 52 weeks: F1 gives nothing; the greatest of the other two, 41.04 from F2 with
-- (9500 + 760) / 250; F3 the greatest where it is (16200 + 400) / 400 = 41.5.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 0 52 9500 760 10 15000 1200 420 20 EQUALS JUST 41.04
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` FALSE 0 FALSE 1800 152 2 9500 760 10 16200 400 420 20 EQUALS JUST 41.5
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly hours` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 0 52 0 0 260 0 0 20 20 EQUALS NOTHING

